Third-party components and their licences
-----------------------------------------

This licence covers the Crucible source. It does not relicense bundled third-party
work, which stays under its own terms and must be preserved by anyone redistributing:

  apps/web/scripts/fonts/BricolageGrotesque-var.ttf
  apps/web/scripts/fonts/JetBrainsMono-var.ttf
      SIL Open Font License 1.1. Full licence text:
      apps/web/scripts/fonts/OFL-bricolage.txt
      apps/web/scripts/fonts/OFL-jetbrains.txt
      These are vendored rather than fetched from a CDN so the product renders the
      same way offline and on a restricted stage network. If you substitute the
      fonts, the wordmark in apps/web/public/og.png and the icon sheet are generated
      from these files by `npm run icons --workspace @crucible/web`.

  crucible-contracts/lib/forge-std
      MIT / Apache-2.0 dual licence, per its own repository. Not vendored into git
      (see .gitignore); fetched with `forge install`.

  All npm dependencies under node_modules/
      Each retains the licence it ships with.
